When generating a Git commit message for this repo (including the Source Control sparkle / suggest commit message), follow Conventional Commits exactly:

<type>[optional scope]: <small description>

Rules:
- One subject line only. No body, no lists, no "Made with Cursor", no quotes.
- type (lowercase): feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert
- Optional scope in parentheses for the area changed, e.g. (audio), (midi), (ui), (clap)
- Description: lowercase, imperative mood, about 50–72 characters, no trailing period
- Match the actual staged diff. Do not mention files unless they are the change.

Examples:
feat(audio): add metronome count-in before record
fix(midi): keep arp latch when clock sync is on
refactor(clap): extract plugin editor into its own module
chore: bump tauri cli to 2.11
